Package: tidesdb-mysql-plugin
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: TidesDB MySQL Maintainers <noreply@tidesdb.example>
Section: database
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/EvgeniyPatlan/tidesdb-mysql
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libsnappy1v5, libzstd1, liblz4-1
Recommends: mysql-server (>= 9.7) | mysql-community-server (>= 9.7)
Description: TidesDB LSM-tree storage engine for MySQL 9.7
 TidesDB-MySQL is a port of the TideSQL storage engine plugin to
 MySQL 9.7 LTS. It exposes the TidesDB LSM-tree key/value engine
 as a loadable storage engine: CREATE TABLE ... ENGINE=TIDESDB.
 .
 Features:
  * Single-column and composite primary keys (incl. AUTO_INCREMENT
    as a non-leading column)
  * Composite secondary indexes with index-condition pushdown
  * 2-phase commit; ER_LOCK_DEADLOCK surfaces cleanly
  * Online DDL: ADD/DROP INDEX (INPLACE), ADD COLUMN /
    trailing DROP COLUMN (INSTANT)
  * AES-256-CBC at-rest encryption via a master-key file
  * Per-table compression: NONE | SNAPPY | LZ4 | ZSTD | LZ4_FAST
  * Cross-restart persistence
  * Mixed-engine transactions (TidesDB + InnoDB in the same BEGIN..COMMIT)
 .
 Install this package alongside mysql-server, then enable the engine
 with INSTALL PLUGIN or by dropping the supplied tidesdb.cnf.example
 into /etc/mysql/conf.d/.
